    title={\Large\bfseries\sffamily Academic Scope and Disclaimer}
]
\sffamily\normalsize\setlength{\parskip}{8pt}

\textbf{1. Pedagogical Intent}\\
This publication is developed as a comprehensive university-level master textbook designed to impart thorough environmental literacy, scientific principles of sustainable resource management, and regulatory compliance knowledge to undergraduate students of engineering and technology.

\textbf{2. Institutional Alignment}\\
Curricular topics, unit structures, and practice question patterns are compiled under educational fair use to assist students in mastering the established syllabus for CHE110.

\textbf{3. Rigor \& Quantitative Precision}\\
Environmental science requires rigorous multidisciplinary synthesis across ecology, chemical engineering, atmospheric dynamics, and jurisprudence. All mathematical formulations and statutory references have been prepared in concordance with standards established by CPCB, MoEFCC, NDMA, and international treaty conventions (UNFCCC, CBD, UNDRR).
\end{tcolorbox}
